ZeroKeyUSB — Licensing
======================

Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Depbit-lab. All rights reserved except as granted below.

ZeroKeyUSB is source-available: every file in this repository is public so
anyone can read, audit, build and modify it. Commercial use of the design and
the code requires a separate commercial license from Depbit-lab.

Required Notice: Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Depbit-lab (https://zerokeyusb.com)


1. Which license applies to what
--------------------------------

  Software — firmware, bootloader, tools and web tools
    (source code, scripts, HTML/JS/CSS and the compiled binaries built from them)
    -> PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0
       LICENSES/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.md
       https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0

  Hardware and documentation — PCB, schematics, BOM, placement files,
    3D models / STL, pictures and written documentation
    -> Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
       (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)
       LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt
       https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

  Third-party components (Arduino core, Adafruit libraries, uBitcoin,
    AES and Base64 code, and the libraries bundled with the web tools)
    -> keep their own licenses. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Nothing in this
       file changes or restricts those licenses.


2. Additional permission for owners of a ZeroKeyUSB device
----------------------------------------------------------

In addition to the licenses above, Depbit-lab grants every person and
organization that owns a genuine ZeroKeyUSB device permission to install and
run the official ZeroKeyUSB firmware and to use the official web tools with
that device for any purpose, including commercial and professional purposes
(for example, using the device to store and type credentials at work).

This permission covers using the device. It does not grant any right to
manufacture, sell, or commercially distribute the hardware design, the
firmware, or products derived from them.


3. Commercial licensing
-----------------------

To manufacture, sell, or otherwise use the ZeroKeyUSB design or code for a
commercial purpose not covered above, contact bruno@zerokeyusb.com.


4. Trademarks
-------------

"ZeroKeyUSB", "ZeroKey" and the ZeroKeyUSB logo are not licensed under any of
the licenses above. Do not use them to identify a product that is not made or
authorized by Depbit-lab.


5. Earlier versions
-------------------

Versions of this repository published before this licensing change were
released under the MIT License, and remain available under the MIT License.
This change applies to the contents of this repository from this commit on.
